  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream main 0757563d; not stacked on #1134, which carries `needs-rework`).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe verifier's crossing law (a) read orientation signs exactly, so two moves meeting at one vertex reached twice, a rounding apart, could read as a proper crossing and hold the post with `Warning::Crossing`.\n\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/laws.rs`: new `pub const CROSSING_TOUCH: f64 = 1e-9` (mm), documented (f64 rounding at 1e4 mm is ~2e-12 mm; cutting tolerances are microns), re-exported as `camcraft_sim::verify::CROSSING_TOUCH`. New `proper_cross_touch`: `proper_cross` with a chord end that stands within `CROSSING_TOUCH` of one of the other chord's **end points** read as on that chord's line (orientation 0, a touch). The test is a point-to-point distance (`hypot`), not a raw cross-product magnitude, so it does not scale with chord length.\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/crossing.rs`: law (a)'s pair predicate asks `proper_cross_touch`. `proper_cross` itself is unchanged, so `dist2_segs` and the arc-wall law keep the exact predicate.\n- Doc comment and decision file say the law is the reference: the planner's `guard::crosses` (#1048, PR #1134's `TOUCH`) should use or match this constant and this end-point reading.\n\n**Why end points, not the line (as #1129's text proposed).** The #1134 review showed that excusing an end within `TOUCH` of the other chord's *line* hides a real pass-through: a walk crossing a chord at a vertex 0.5 pm off its interior makes both of its chords there read as touches. That review said #1129 must not port that test to the verifier. Every case the issue names is a shared vertex, so the end-point reading fixes them and keeps that probe reported. Recorded in `docs/decisions/1129-crossing-tolerance.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPins, `crates/sim/tests/crossing_touch.rs` (each checks the bucketed law against the all-pairs reference):\n- `a_shared_vertex_a_rounding_apart_does_not_warn`: a joint 1e-12 mm apart in 16 directions, origins 0 / 37.25 / 1000 mm, chords 1 um / 0.5 / 20 / 1000 mm. Each scale asserts the old exact test tripped on at least one jitter. This test fails with the old predicate (checked).\n- `a_crossing_a_micron_through_still_warns`: same scales, B starting 1 um short of A's end and 1 um below its line (a quarter chord for the 1 um chord).\n- `a_walk_through_a_chord_at_a_vertex_a_picometre_off_its_line_still_warns`: the #1134 review's probe, vertex at -0.5 / +0.5 pm, at y 0 and 1000 mm.\n- `collinear_overlaps_keep_their_reading`: partly overlapping collinear chords at 4 angles and 3 scales give the exact-sign verdict; an exact retrace stays no crossing.\n- `a_joint_just_past_the_touch_keeps_the_exact_reading`: at 2e-9 mm the exact verdict is kept, so the edge itself is pinned.\n\nGate (macOS arm64, debug):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim`: lib and all 58 test binaries green (incl. `crossing_touch` 5, `crossing_buckets` 3).\n- `camcraft-app`: `verify` 21 (2 ignored), `golden_cl` 25, `verify_arc_reading` 7, `carried_verify` 8, `warned_moves` 2, `operations` 117 (6 ignored), `solid_law_goldens` 5, `shoulder_adaptive` 3, `trochoid_op` 5, `pocket3d_hsm` 1 (1 ignored): all pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib adaptive`: 26 passed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNo existing verify test or golden changed verdict.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The planner side: `motion` `adaptive::guard` is untouched. PR #1134 should adopt `CROSSING_TOUCH` and the end-point reading when it is reworked.\n- The release `--ignored` heavy lanes and the UI suites were not run.\n- Residual, same in kind as before: two walks crossing in an X exactly through a shared vertex were never reported by the exact-sign law; this extends that reading to a vertex a picometre apart. No new class of miss.\n\nChangelog: The verifier's crossing law no longer holds the post when two moves share a vertex a rounding apart (within 1e-9 mm); a real crossing, including a pass-through at a vertex near another chord's interior, still blocks (#1129).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1129\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
